<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-4239] Public thread pool starvation is cause of deadlock when user&apos;s jobs calls cache.size()</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-4239</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The users job are hang when a lot of jobs that calculates cache size are submitted.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The log contains message:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;WARNING: Possible thread pool starvation detected (no task completed in last 30000ms, is executorService pool size large enough?)
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;After a while all the thread of a public thread pool are locked on waiting the SizeTask future. &lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="13021356">IGNITE-4239</key>
            <summary>Public thread pool starvation is cause of deadlock when user&apos;s jobs calls cache.size()</summary>
